Q5. Calculate Simple Interest
Question:
Write a program to calculate simple interest and the total amount using the principal amount, annual interest rate, and time period.

Sample Input:
Principal = 50000
Rate = 8
Time = 3


Expected Output:
Simple Interest = 12000
Total Amount = 62000


Formula:
- Simple Interest = (Principal × Rate × Time) / 100
- Total Amount = Principal + Simple Interest
Python Code:
principal = 50000rate = 8time = 3simple_interest = (principal * rate * time) / 100total_amount = principal + simple_interestprint("Simple Interest =", simple_interest)print("Total Amount =", total_amount)



C Code:
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    float principal = 50000;
    float rate = 8;
    float time = 3;

    float simple_interest =
        (principal * rate * time) / 100;

    float total_amount = principal + simple_interest;

    printf("Simple Interest = %.0f\n", simple_interest);
    printf("Total Amount = %.0f\n", total_amount);

    return 0;
}


Java Code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double principal = 50000;
        double rate = 8;
        double time = 3;

        double simpleInterest =
            (principal * rate * time) / 100;

        double totalAmount = principal + simpleInterest;

        System.out.println("Simple Interest = " + simpleInterest);
        System.out.println("Total Amount = " + totalAmount);
    }
}

